<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea Shipping - Steel scrap cargoes - June 25.</title>
<headline>S.Korea Shipping - Steel scrap cargoes - June 25.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the arrival schedule for major steel scrap vessels unloading at South Korean ports of Inchon, Pusan, Masan, Pohang, Kwangyang and Asan, as detailed on Wednesday by South Korean surveyors.</p>
<p>-- INCHON PORT</p>
<p> VESSEL	    TONNE    ETA	  ETD	  BUYER</p>
<p> Jade Pacific    32,000   June 25		   Inchon</p>
<p> Canavera	  40,000   July 5		    Inchon</p>
<p> Rova		38,391   Mid-July		  Inchon</p>
<p> Feng Shou	 50,000   July 15		   Inchon</p>
<p>-- PUSAN PORT</p>
<p> Delta-Trident   35,000   June 14    July 2     Dongkuk</p>
<p>-- MASAN PORT</p>
<p> Venus	     39,185   June 14    July 1     KISCO</p>
<p>-- POHANG PORT</p>
<p> Quatetdla	 22,500   July 10		   POSCO</p>
<p> Caspian-Trident 38,000   July 21		   POSCO</p>
<p> Seabee1	   30,000   Mid-July		  POSCO</p>
<p>-- KWANGYANG PORT</p>
<p> Faethon	   30,000   July 5		    POSCO</p>
<p> Cupa		22,000   July 6		    POSCO</p>
<p> Feng Yao	  50,000   July 15		   POSCO</p>
<p> Al Qawiyyu	30,000   July 16		   POSCO</p>
<p> Lok Kranti	31,000   July 24		   POSCO</p>
<p> Xing Su Hai     30,000   July 30		   POSCO</p>
<p>-- ASAN PORT</p>
<p> Orhan Ekinci    33,474   June 18    June 27    Hanbo</p>
<p> Cenk-Kaptanoglu 31,407   June 19    July 1     Hanbo</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
